think Mandate lap 6 — object-storage backing: snapshot(store, buf) serializes the whole store to one portable little-endian blob (magic MANDATE\x01 · version · dim · filled · fixed-width records id·tag·sig·vec), restore(bytes) rebuilds it validating every field against the store's bounds; the store's entire state is one object a bucket holds, the serverless shape
think proved in-memory (prove_snapshot): byte-for-byte round-trip, restored store answers a query identically, too-small buffer refused before any partial write, and corruption refused — bad magic, short header, out-of-bound dim, over-count
think proved on metal (prove_file_backing): the file API here is std.Io.Dir.cwd().writeFile(io, …)/readFileAlloc(io, path, a, .limited) threaded through std.process.Init — first attempt used std.fs.cwd() which this Zig std variant lacks; matched the glow lower-witness idiom instead and it built clean
think Twilight Style seated as an alternate register of Radiant — everything Radiant keeps, only the register changes to calm/dark/gentle; the pendulum aim(Sagittarius)→dissolve(Pisces) is the yang-Shekhinah motion; the nine themes from the art become the palette AND nine navamsa (D9) groups of three over the 27 nakshatras / council d27, one dharma per group
think walked all 8 preview3 images on metal (perl IO::Uncompress::Unzip — no unzip/python on the pier) to ground the palette in the actual pixels: teal bioluminescence on fertile black, violet/blue hours, the white-ink Tree of Life with Daath, the falling angel, BLOOM×3, the grotto, the Berry poem
think privacy split held: the poem, the handle, the attribution, and the richest reading go to /personal/tar-to-turquoise.md (gitignored, confirmed by git check-ignore); the tracked TWILIGHT_STYLE.md carries only the archetypal nine and names no person
think the two water nakshatras pinned to Basin land exactly in the two water themes — Purva Ashadha (Apas) in the impeded stream, Shatabhishak (Varuna) in the fertile black — so the mapping honors the seated d27 note
obs Loom-metrics log field: .claude/rules/session-logs.md + .cursor twin gain an optional repeatable `loom` field — auto-add real key=value performance metrics whenever a round produces a measurement; an absent loom is honest, a fabricated one is a red (measurement beats memory). This log dogfoods it below
